\ fit-nonnegative ( X y -- beta ): nonnegative least squares, Lawson-Hanson.
\ fit-simplex ( X y -- weights ): weights >= 0 summing to 1 (one rounding).
"statistics" load-library

\ === fit-nonnegative ===
\ identity design: y passes through with negatives clamped to exact 0
[ 1 0 0 1 ] 2 2 matrix [ 0.3 -0.9 ] vector fit-nonnegative matrix>array . cr  \ [ 0.3 0 ]
[ 1 0 0 1 ] 2 2 matrix [ -1 -0.5 ] vector fit-nonnegative matrix>array . cr  \ [ 0 0 ]

\ suppression design: x1 enters on the larger raw gradient, the joint solve
\ sends it negative, the feasibility loop demotes it (the inner-loop path)
[ 10 0.5 0 0.8660254037844386 ] 2 2 matrix to X
[ 0.2 1.0392304845413263 ] vector to y
X y fit-linear matrix>array [: 100 * round :] map . cr   \ [ -4 120 ] — OLS goes negative
X y fit-nonnegative to beta
beta matrix>array . cr                                   \ [ 0 1 ]

\ KKT at the answer: beta >= 0, passive gradient ~0, active gradient <= 0
beta min 0 >= . cr                                       \ 1
X transpose  y X beta matmul -  matmul to kkt
kkt 0 @e -3 0.0001 expect-near                           \ active: -3 <= 0
kkt 1 @e 0 1e-10 expect-near "kkt holds" . cr            \ kkt holds

\ correlated 6x2 design: OLS negative, nnls zeroes the suppressed column
[ 1 1 1 1.05 1 0.95 1 1 1 1.02 1 0.98 ] 6 2 matrix to X
[ 1 2.2 -0.1 1.1 2.0 0.1 ] vector to y
X y fit-nonnegative to beta
beta matrix>array [: 1e6 * round :] map . cr             \ [ 0 1074461 ]
X transpose  y X beta matmul -  matmul 1 @e 0 1e-9 expect-near "passive flat" . cr

\ === fit-simplex ===
\ interior: the simplex projection of (0.3, 0.9) is (0.2, 0.8)
[ 1 0 0 1 ] 2 2 matrix [ 0.3 0.9 ] vector fit-simplex to w
w matrix>array [: 1e6 * round :] map . cr                \ [ 200000 800000 ] — the mu-penalty leaves ~3e-8 per weight
w sum 1 1e-12 expect-near "sums to one" . cr             \ sums to one

\ boundary of nothing: projection of (-1, -0.5) keeps both coordinates positive
[ 1 0 0 1 ] 2 2 matrix [ -1 -0.5 ] vector fit-simplex matrix>array . cr  \ [ 0.25 0.75 ]

\ y inside the column hull: exact barycentric weights, zero residual
[ 0 1 1 0 ] 2 2 matrix [ 0.25 0.75 ] vector fit-simplex matrix>array . cr  \ [ 0.75 0.25 ]

\ suppression design again: all weight on the second column
[ 10 0.5 0 0.8660254037844386 ] 2 2 matrix
[ 0.2 1.0392304845413263 ] vector fit-simplex matrix>array . cr  \ [ 0 1 ]

\ === random designs: KKT verified whatever path the solver took ===
: kkt-holds | design response |
	design response fit-nonnegative to solution
	solution min 0 >= expect
	design transpose  response design solution matmul -  matmul to gradient
	gradient max  design transpose response matmul abs max 1e-8 *  <= expect ;

42 seed
[: drop
	[: drop random 2 * 1 - :] 60 iota swap map vector 20 3 reshape
	[: drop random 2 * 1 - :] 20 iota swap map vector
	kkt-holds
:] 5 i-times
"random kkt ok" . cr                                     \ random kkt ok

\ === errors ===
\ run-libs requires exit 0 of a golden-bearing test, so the error is caught
clear
[: [ 1 0 0 1 ] 2 2 matrix [ 1 2 3 ] vector fit-nonnegative :]
[: . cr :] try-catch                \ the lib matmul throws its message string
